«
@@ DMOPendulum — demo of uncertainty on an equation of the Equation
@@ Library, Simple Pendulum: its period for small amplitudes,
@@ T = 2π√(L/g), and its real period Treal = T·Σ(x;0;5;c(x)²·sin(θmax/2)^(2x)),
@@ with c(x) = (2x)!/(2^x·x!)². L is drawn from a normal law, 15±σ0.1 cm,
@@ and the amplitude θmax from a rectangular law over a range of 20°, drawn
@@ at random from 0…20° to 60…80°, or given as { lo hi } in degrees.
@@ 300 draws (fewer if they take more than about 30 s, 30 at least,
@@ unless the global variable ExtendedTrials is not 0): the histograms of
@@ T (gray) and Treal (black) on the same axis; Treal is then compared
@@ with the linear propagation of σRFxjxi, for independent inputs whatever
@@ the variable ρij holds.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @ The range of θmax, if given; any other object is left alone
  0
  If Depth 1 > Then Drop Dup TypeName End
  → dmpty
  «
  If dmpty "list" == Then
    Dup 1 Get Swap 2 Get
  Else
    RAND 13 * IP R→I 5 * Dup 20 +
  End
  300 9.80665
  @ The squared coefficients c(x)² of the series, x = 0 … 5
  { 1 0.25 0.140625 0.09765625 0.07476806640625 0.0605621337890625 }
  → dmpt0 dmpt1 dmpn dmpg dmpc
  «
    ClΣ
    @ Up to 300 draws, but no longer than about 30 s, and 30 at least:
    @ NormlRand is slow on a calculator. ExtendedTrials other than 0 asks
    @ for the 300 draws whatever the time.
    IfErr 'ExtendedTrials' Rcl Then Drop 0 End 0 ≠
    Ticks 0
    → dmpext dmptk0 dmpk
    «
      Do
        0.15 0.001 ⓁNormlRand
        RAND dmpt1 dmpt0 - * dmpt0 + 1_° * 2 / Sin Sq
        → dmpl dmpu
        «
          @ T, then the series by Horner's rule, from c(5)² down to c(0)²
          2 π →Num * dmpl dmpg / √ *
          Dup
          0 6 1 For dmpj dmpu * dmpc dmpj Get + -1 Step
          *
          2 →Array Σ+
        »
        dmpk 1 + 'dmpk' Sto
      Until
        dmpk dmpn ≥
        dmpext Not dmpk 30 ≥ And Ticks dmptk0 - 30000 > And Or
      End
      dmpk 'dmpn' Sto
    »
    @ The two columns: their means and standard deviations
    Average StandardDeviation MinΣ MaxΣ
    → dmpm dmpd dmplo dmphi
    «
      dmplo 1 Get dmphi 2 Get
      → dmpa dmpb
      «
        dmpb dmpa - 0.04 *
        → dmpe
        «
          dmpa dmpe - dmpb dmpe +
          → dmpx0 dmpx1
          «
            @ 40 classes for 300 draws, fewer for fewer draws, 8 at least
            dmpx1 dmpx0 - dmpn √ 2.31 * IP 8 Max 40 Min /
            → dmpw
            «
              dmpn dmpw * dmpd 1 Get 2.5066 * / 2.2 *
              → dmpy
              «
                ClearLCD
                dmpx0 dmpx1 XRange dmpy -12 / dmpy YRange dmpw Res
                @ Each column alone: HistogramPlot takes the first column
                @ Treal first, then T over it, which shows when they coincide
                RclΣ TRN
                Dup 2 Get HistogramPlot
                1 Get 0.5 Gray Foreground HistogramPlot 'Foreground' Purge
                'PPAR' Purge
                @ The Monte Carlo results, written at once
                "Pendulum: L=15±σ0.1 cm, θmax " dmpt0 →Text + "…" + dmpt1 →Text + "°" +
                { #0d #0d 0 true false } DrawText
                "T " dmpm 1 Get 3 RND →Text + "±σ" + dmpd 1 Get 4 RND →Text + " s (gray)" +
                { #0d #18d 0 true false } DrawText
                "Treal " dmpm 2 Get 3 RND →Text + "±σ" + dmpd 2 Get 4 RND →Text + " s (MC, " + dmpn →Text + " draws)" +
                { #0d #36d 0 true false } DrawText
                dmpx0 3 RND →Text " s" + { #0d #222d 0 true false } DrawText
                dmpx1 3 RND →Text " s" + { #340d #222d 0 true false } DrawText
                @ Treal by the linear propagation of σRFxjxi: θmax as the
                @ centre of its range ±σ its width/√12. The inputs are
                @ independent: a variable ρij left by another calculation
                @ is set aside, then put back.
                IfErr 'ρij' Rcl 1 Then Drop 0 0 End
                → dmprho dmphad
                «
                  IfErr { ρij } Purge Then End
                  '2*π*√(x2/9.80665)*(1+0.25*sin(x1/2)^2+0.140625*sin(x1/2)^4+0.09765625*sin(x1/2)^6+0.07476806640625*sin(x1/2)^8+0.0605621337890625*sin(x1/2)^10)'
                  0.15±σ0.001
                  dmpt0 dmpt1 + 2 / →Num →Text "±σ" + dmpt1 dmpt0 - 12 √ / →Num →Text + "_°" + Str→
                  ⓁσRFxjxi →Num
                  If dmphad Then dmprho 'ρij' Sto End
                »
                → dmplin
                «
                  dmplin Explode
                  → dmpla dmplb
                  «
                    "Treal " dmpla 3 RND →Text + "±σ" + dmplb 4 RND →Text + " s (linear)" +
                    { #0d #54d 0 true false } DrawText
                  »
                  dmpm 1 Get dmpd 1 Get 2 →List "T MC" →Tag
                  dmpm 2 Get dmpd 2 Get 2 →List "Treal MC" →Tag
                  dmplin "Treal linear" →Tag
                »
              »
            »
          »
        »
      »
    »
  »
  »
»
